"FUTURE FEATURE (user, 2026-08-13): track locations each player has visited and visually mark paths leading toward previously visited rooms. Design notes: a JOIN TABLE VisitedLocation { player_entity_id, location_entity_id } with BTREE INDEXES ON BOTH COLUMNS (user suggestion) -- player-indexed for the client's own-subscription and marker lookups, location-indexed for cleanup. Recording: idempotent insert on player location change (a small system pass over player locations, or hooks at the three location-writing sites: move effect, respawn, activation). CLEANUP: when map-instance teardown deletes a room, delete its visited rows via the location index -- markers must never outlive the room (a regenerated map has NEW room entity ids, so stale markers cannot lie); player deletion cleans via the player index. CLIENT: subscribe own visited rows; a path marks as 'toward visited' when its destination room id is in the set (works for intra-map and materialized cross-map paths alike). No gameplay mechanics attached -- purely a wayfinding aid."